// parts-db.mjs — component database + designator-pattern classifier for the Traction Inverter.
// One row per part family: m = designator regex (FIRST MATCH WINS — specific above catch-all),
// mpn/mfr/desc/fp, lcsc where a specific orderable part was verified (else CLASS = buy to the
// stated rating), price1k = INR at ~1k-inverter aggregate (planning figure, RFQ ±30 %),
// alt = second-source CANDIDATE in the same footprint: qualify before use, never an automatic
// drop-in (round 12, R1-F11 — a slow rectifier or a 3-lead FET in a 4-lead pad is not a substitute).
//
// Sources: hiitio catalog research 2026-09-09 (HCS600FH120D3C1 module line, HCM75S12T4K3),
// NXP EV-INVERTERGEN3 schematics (SPF-91122 / SPF-88955 — exact MPNs read off the sheets),
// Wolfspeed XM3 discharge PCB (CRGP2512F68K network), TI TIDM-02014, DC-Modules platform
// (NSI6611 verified pin map, LCSC codes carried over where the same part is reused).

export const OVERRIDES = {};   // per-designator {mpn} overrides (none yet)

// Rows printed on the power sheet's safety/discharge panels (kicad5-gen consumes these).
// ---- platform SKUs (review A.6): ONE power PCB, ONE control card, ONE discharge PCB, ONE
// cap-bank busbar drawing. A SKU = base DB + these rows (first match wins). A row's `value`
// replaces the drawn value in that SKU's BOM, so value and MPN can never disagree (bom-gen
// fails the build if they do). The drawn schematic is the SiC-8XX build.
// Silicon: HCG600FH120D3E1EA shares the D3 outline and the 11-pin map of HCS600FH120D3C1
// (DS p.8: 1=G_L 2=E_L 3=DC- 4=DC+ 5/6=NTC 7=G_H 8=E_H 9=HS C-sense 10/11=AC).
// Bus: 4XX swaps the 16 film cans for a 600 V class in the SAME 37.5 mm positions and
// rescales the discharge resistors on the same discharge PCB.
